{"type":"text","timestamp":1787411293038,"sessionID":"ses_fd5fe494dffepH7br4dzOR1vci","part":{"id":"prt_02a03dde90010xPyE5jZNQkPvo","messageID":"msg_02a03d062001Yko6C0mi7tSOcD","sessionID":"ses_fd5fe494dffepH7br4dzOR1vci","type":"text","text":"The 5 failures in `range.test.js` are pre-existing (present before my change) and unrelated to `coerce`. My change is the only modification and stays within the editable scope.\n\nThe implementation:\n- `functions/coerce.js:22` — non-rtl now uses `COERCEFULL` when `includePrerelease` is set (adds prerelease/build groups).\n- `functions/coerce.js:25-49` — `rtl` walks the global `COERCERTL`/`COERCERTLFULL` regex, manually advancing `lastIndex` to capture overlapping matches and keeping the right-most non-shared-terminus triple; `lastIndex` is reset to `-1` so repeated calls are deterministic.\n- `functions/coerce.js:51-59` — carries `prerelease`/`build` through only when `includePrerelease` is set, composing with `rtl`.\n\nAll task examples verified: `1.2.3.4`→`2.3.4`, `1.2.3.4.5`→`3.4.5`, `1.2.3-alpha.1+build.2`→`1.2.3-alpha.1` (build `[\"build\",\"2\"]`), `1.2.3.4-rc`+rtl+includePrerelease→`2.3.4-rc`; passthrough, numeric, and null cases unchanged; repeat calls stable.","time":{"start":1787411291625,"end":1787411293032}}}
